# Service evolution and migration

A consuming team needs a new cents-based response while an old client still expects yuan. Preserve IDs and both versioned contracts.

## Input and contract
input/fixture.json; input/dictionary.md; project version 1

## Finding and reproducible output
```json
{
  "v1": [
    {
      "id": "L1",
      "total": 120.99
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "total": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "total": 8.01
    }
  ],
  "v2": [
    {
      "id": "L1",
      "totalCents": 12099,
      "currency": "CNY"
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "totalCents": 0,
      "currency": "CNY"
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "totalCents": 801,
      "currency": "CNY"
    }
  ],
  "preservedIds": [
    "L1",
    "L2",
    "L3"
  ],
  "invalid": []
}
```

## Failure prevented
Changing the old client to cents without a version change breaks compatibility.

